## 1. DEFINITIONS

**1.1** "Devs" refers to Devs Corporation and its affiliates, subsidiaries, partners, authorized distributors, resellers, and representatives.

**1.2** "Licensed Products" means all software programs, applications, utilities, tools, firmware, drivers, middleware, development kits, APIs, libraries, frameworks, and physical hardware components including but not limited to PC parts, processors, graphics cards, motherboards, memory modules, storage devices, cooling systems, power supplies, peripherals, accessories, and computing devices manufactured, distributed, sold, or licensed by Devs.

**1.3** "You" or "Licensee" refers to the individual, corporation, partnership, organization, educational institution, government entity, or other legal entity that has acquired, downloaded, purchased, leased, or otherwise obtained Licensed Products from Devs or its authorized channels.

**1.4** "Documentation" means any user guides, technical manuals, API documentation, specifications, white papers, installation guides, troubleshooting guides, video tutorials, or other materials provided by Devs relating to Licensed Products.

**1.5** "Authorized Device" means a single physical or virtual computer, workstation, server, mobile device, embedded system, or other computing device on which Licensed Products are installed, activated, or used.

**1.6** "Educational Software" means any software tools, trainers, debuggers, memory editors, or analysis programs developed by Devs for educational, research, security testing, or academic purposes only.

**1.7** "Source Code" means the human-readable form of software code, including all comments, documentation, and related development materials.

**1.8** "End User" means the final user of Licensed Products who is not reselling or redistributing such products.

**1.9** "Commercial Use" means use of Licensed Products in any business, commercial enterprise, for-profit activity, or revenue-generating operation.

**1.10** "Confidential Information" means any proprietary or non-public information disclosed by Devs, including trade secrets, technical specifications, roadmaps, pricing, and business strategies.

