## 2. GRANT OF LICENSE

**2.1 Software License**  
Subject to the terms of this Agreement, Devs grants you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to install and use Licensed Software Products solely for your internal business, educational, research, or personal purposes on Authorized Devices in accordance with the license tier you have purchased.

**2.2 Hardware License**  
Purchase of Devs hardware components grants you ownership of the physical hardware, subject to the warranty terms and restrictions outlined in this Agreement. Firmware, embedded software, microcode, and BIOS/UEFI software in hardware remain licensed, not sold, and are subject to the software license terms herein.

**2.3 License Tiers**

**2.3.1 Personal License**
- Installation on up to three (3) Authorized Devices per license key
- Use by a single user or household
- Non-commercial purposes only
- No redistribution rights

**2.3.2 Professional License**
- Installation on up to ten (10) Authorized Devices
- Commercial use permitted for individual contractors or small teams (up to 5 users)
- Limited redistribution of runtime components as specified in Documentation
- Technical support included

**2.3.3 Enterprise License**
- Unlimited installations within a single organization
- Full commercial use rights
- Site-wide deployment permitted
- Priority technical support and dedicated account management
- Beta access to new features
- Custom integration support available

**2.3.4 Educational License**
- Special pricing for accredited educational institutions
- Installation on classroom and lab computers
- Use restricted to educational and non-commercial research purposes
- Student projects permitted under supervision

**2.3.5 OEM License**
- For hardware manufacturers bundling Devs software
- Distribution rights as specified in separate OEM agreement
- Custom branding options available

**2.4 Trial and Evaluation Licenses**  
Devs may offer time-limited trial versions with reduced functionality. Trial licenses automatically expire after the evaluation period and require purchase for continued use.

**2.5 Open Source Components**  
Some Licensed Products may include open source software components governed by separate licenses. Such components are licensed under their respective terms, which are provided in the Documentation.

