## 7. SOFTWARE SUPPORT AND MAINTENANCE

**7.1 Software Updates**  
Devs may provide updates, patches, bug fixes, security updates, or new versions of Licensed Software Products. Such updates may be:
- Automatically downloaded and installed on your Authorized Devices
- Made available through the Devs Update Manager
- Delivered through subscription-based update services
- Required for continued use of online features or license validation

**7.2 Update Types**

**7.2.1 Critical Security Updates**  
Security patches addressing vulnerabilities will be provided to all active licensees regardless of support status.

**7.2.2 Feature Updates**  
New features and major version upgrades may require:
- Active maintenance subscription
- Upgrade fee payment
- Migration to newer license terms

**7.2.3 Compatibility Updates**  
Updates to maintain compatibility with operating system updates, hardware changes, or third-party software.

**7.3 Technical Support**

**7.3.1 Community Support (Free)**
- Access to community forums and knowledge base
- User-generated documentation and tutorials
- Email support with 5-7 business day response time

**7.3.2 Standard Support (Included with Professional)**
- Email and chat support with 2-3 business day response
- Access to technical documentation
- Bug fix priority
- Phone support during business hours

**7.3.3 Premium Support (Enterprise)**
- 24/7 phone, email, and chat support
- 4-hour response time for critical issues
- Dedicated support engineer
- Remote assistance and on-site support options
- Access to beta programs and early releases

**7.4 End of Life Policy**  
Devs will provide notice at least six (6) months before discontinuing support for any Licensed Product version. After end-of-life date:
- No further updates will be provided
- Technical support will not be available
- License validation may cease to function
- Migration tools to newer versions may be offered

**7.5 Compatibility**  
Devs does not guarantee that updates will maintain compatibility with:
- Unsupported operating systems or hardware configurations
- Third-party software, plugins, or extensions
- Custom modifications or configurations
- Legacy file formats or data structures

