## 24. DISPUTE RESOLUTION

**24.1 Informal Resolution**  
Before initiating formal proceedings, parties agree to attempt good faith negotiations to resolve disputes. Either party may initiate by written notice to the other, and parties will meet within thirty (30) days.

**24.2 Binding Arbitration**  
Any disputes not resolved informally shall be resolved through binding arbitration administered by the American Arbitration Association (AAA) under its Commercial Arbitration Rules.

**24.3 Arbitration Procedures**
- Location: [Your City, State/Country]
- Arbitrator: Single arbitrator mutually agreed upon, or appointed by AAA
- Language: English
- Discovery: Limited to efficiency
- Costs: Each party bears own costs unless arbitrator rules otherwise
- Award: Final, binding, and enforceable in any court of competent jurisdiction

**24.4 Class Action Waiver**  
YOU AGREE THAT DISPUTES WILL BE RESOLVED INDIVIDUALLY, NOT AS A CLASS ACTION, CONSOLIDATED ACTION, OR REPRESENTATIVE ACTION. YOU WAIVE ANY RIGHT TO PARTICIPATE IN CLASS ACTIONS AGAINST DEVS.

**24.5 Small Claims Exception**  
Either party may bring an individual action in small claims court for matters within its jurisdiction.

**24.6 Injunctive Relief**  
Nothing prevents either party from seeking injunctive or other equitable relief in court for:
- Intellectual property infringement
- Breach of confidentiality
- Misuse of Educational Software
- Threats to data security or business operations

**24.7 Opt-Out**  
You may opt out of arbitration by written notice to legal@devs.com within thirty (30) days of first accepting this Agreement. Opt-out does not affect other provisions.

