**25.1 Governing Law**  
This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of [Your State/Country], without regard to conflict of law principles. The United Nations Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods does not apply.

**25.2 Jurisdiction and Venue**  
Except for matters subject to arbitration, exclusive jurisdiction and venue for any legal proceedings shall be the state and federal courts located in [Your County, State], and parties consent to personal jurisdiction in such courts.

**25.3 Severability**  
If any provision of this Agreement is found invalid, illegal, or unenforceable by a court of competent jurisdiction, such provision shall be modified to the minimum extent necessary to make it valid and enforceable. If modification is not possible, the provision shall be severed, and the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.

**25.4 Entire Agreement**  
This Agreement, together with the Privacy Policy, any separate written agreements between you and Devs, and Documentation, constitutes the entire agreement between you and Devs regarding Licensed Products and supersedes all prior or contemporaneous agreements, understandings, communications, and proposals, whether oral or written.

**25.5 Amendment**  
Devs reserves the right to modify this Agreement at any time. Changes will be effective:
- Immediately upon posting for material changes affecting security or legal compliance
- Thirty (30) days after notice for all other changes

Notice will be provided through:
- Email to your registered address
- In-product notifications
- Posting on devs.com/legal

Continued use of Licensed Products after changes constitutes acceptance. If you do not agree, you must stop using Licensed Products and may be entitled to a pro-rata refund of prepaid fees.

**25.6 Waiver**  
Failure by Devs to enforce any provision of this Agreement shall not constitute a waiver of that provision or any other provision. No waiver shall be effective unless in writing and signed by an authorized representative of Devs.

**25.7 Assignment**  
You may not assign, transfer, delegate, or sublicense this Agreement or any rights or obligations hereunder without Devs' prior written consent. Any attempted assignment in violation of this provision is void. Devs may assign this Agreement at any time without restriction, including in connection with a merger, acquisition, reorganization, or sale of assets.

**25.8 Notices**  
All notices under this Agreement must be in writing and sent to:

**To Devs:**
Devs Corporation  
Legal Department  
[Your Address]  
[City, State ZIP]  
Email: legal@devs.com

**To You:**
To the email address associated with your account or provided during purchase

Notices are effective upon receipt or, if by email, within two (2) business days of sending.

**25.9 Relationship of Parties**  
This Agreement does not create any partnership, joint venture, employment, agency, or franchise relationship. Neither party has authority to bind the other or incur obligations on the other's behalf.

**25.10 Third-Party Beneficiaries**  
Except for Devs Parties who are express third-party beneficiaries of indemnification provisions, there are no third-party beneficiaries to this Agreement.

**25.11 Interpretation**  
Headings are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation. "Including" means "including without limitation." No presumption applies against the drafting party.

**25.12 Language**  
This Agreement is drafted in English. Any translations are for convenience only. In case of conflict, the English version controls.

**25.13 Survival**  
Provisions that by their nature should survive termination shall survive, including but not limited to: intellectual property rights, confidentiality, indemnification, limitation of liability, dispute resolution, and general provisions.

**25.14 Statute of Limitations**  
Any claim arising under this Agreement must be brought within one (1) year after the claim arises, or such claim is permanently barred.

**25.15 Equitable Remedies**  
You acknowledge that breach of this Agreement may cause irreparable harm to Devs for which monetary damages are inadequate. Devs is entitled to seek equitable relief, including injunctions and specific performance, without posting bond.

**25.16 Attorney Fees**  
In any proceeding to enforce this Agreement, the prevailing party is entitled to recover reasonable attorneys' fees, expert fees, and costs.

**25.17 Electronic Signatures**  
